Package: BayesAiken
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Aiken's V Coefficient with Dirichlet-Multinomial Model
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2025-01-09
Authors@R: person("Jose", "Ventura-Leon",
                  email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
Author: Jose Ventura-Leon [aut, cre] (<https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2996-4244>)
Maintainer: Jose Ventura-Leon <jventuraleon@gmail.com>
Description: Calculates Bayesian credible intervals for Aiken's V coefficient
    using two models: Beta-Binomial (standard) and Dirichlet-Multinomial
    (conservative, recommended for small panels). The Dirichlet-Multinomial
    approach treats each judge as a single observation rather than inflating
    effective sample size, producing wider and more honest intervals when
    expert panels are small (n < 10). Provides posterior means, HDI and ETI
    credible intervals, threshold exceedance probabilities P(V > 0.70),
    and publication-ready visualizations comparing both models.
    Based on Ventura-Leon (2025) "A Dirichlet-Multinomial Framework for
    Bayesian Aiken's V in Content Validity Studies with Small Expert Panels".
